masque-go cmd/client changes for interop/run.sh (docs/interop.md). Applied with
`git apply` on the pinned tag in Dockerfile.peers. The library and cmd/proxy are
unchanged; so is the client's protocol behaviour.

1. `-ca FILE`: trust our test certificate for the proxy and for the target (the stock
   client uses the system roots only).
2. The response body goes to stdout as raw bytes, so the cell can hash it (the stock
   client logs it with log.Println, which adds a timestamp and a newline).
3. Before exit, close the tunnelled HTTP/3 connection with H3_NO_ERROR, wait 200 ms
   for its CONNECTION_CLOSE datagram to leave, then close the CONNECT-UDP stream and
   the proxy connection (the stock client exits without closing anything; run.sh
   requires each connection to our server to close cleanly in time).

